-9720-52ee-964f-785229f9c88c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096070 #edb/ref 1080 "Converges to $1$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096070 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096070 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "4c47b773-49e9-590f-8580-f995e2dca36d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096071 #edb/ref 1080 "The sequence diverges" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096071 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096071 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "57a855bb-1f85-5ab6-93a6-841887543ac6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096551 #edb/ref 1069 "e-646" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096551 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the following sequence: \n\n$$\na_{n+1} = -2a_n, \\qquad a_1 = -4, \\qquad n\\geq 1.\n$$\n\nDetermine whether the sequence is convergent or divergent. If it converges, find the limit." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096551 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "bc0f8f02-ba1c-59c7-ba27-cb2148f2a9f8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096551 #edb/ref 1074 "Suppose we have a geometric sequence with the first term $a_1$ and common ratio $r.$ Then, we have the following convergence properties:\n\n- if $|r| <      1,$ the sequence is convergent and converges to $0$\n\n- if $|r| > 1,$ the sequence is divergent\n\nMoreover, we have the following edge cases:\n\n- if $r=1,$ the sequence is convergent and converges to $a_1$\n\n- if $r= -1,$ the sequence is divergent\n\nThe given sequence is a geometric sequence with the common ratio \n\n$$\nr=\\dfrac{a_{n+1}}{a_n}= -2.\n$$\n\nSince $|r| >1$, the sequence diverges." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096604 #edb/ref 1069 "e-9964" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096604 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the following geometric sequence:\n\n$$\n6, \\quad -2, \\quad \\dfrac{2}{3}, \\quad -\\dfrac{2}{9}, \\quad \\ldots\n$$\n\nDetermine whether the sequence is convergent or divergent. If it converges, find the limit." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096604 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "90ed1cce-a831-58b0-942a-d8b9a17583cc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096604 #edb/ref 1074 "Suppose we have a geometric sequence with the first term $a_1$ and common ratio $r.$ Then, we have the following convergence properties:\n\n- if $|r| <    1,$ the sequence is convergent and converges to $0$\n\n- if $|r| > 1,$ the sequence is divergent\n\nMoreover, we have the following edge cases:\n\n- if $r=1,$ the sequence is convergent and converges to $a_1$\n\n- if $r = -1,$ the sequence is divergent\n\nThe  given sequence is a geometric sequence with the common ratio \n\n$$\nr=\\dfrac{a_2}{a_1}=\\dfrac{(-2)}{6}= -\\dfrac{1}{3}.\n$$\n\nSince $|r| = \\dfrac{1}{3} <      1,$ the sequence converges to $0.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096605 #edb/ref 1069 "e-9989" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096605 #edb/ref 1071 "Does the sequence $a_n=\\left( \\dfrac{5}{3}\\right)^{n-1}$ for $n\\geq  1$ \nconverge or diverge? If it converges, what is its limit?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096605 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0bbb71a2-ff71-5f25-80bc-e56bbed9ac1f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096605 #edb/ref 1074 "Suppose we have a geometric sequence with the first term $a_1$ and common ratio $r.$ Then, we have the following convergence properties:\n\n- if $|r| <      1,$ the sequence is convergent and converges to $0$\n\n- if $|r| > 1,$ the sequence is divergent\n\nMoreover, we have the following edge cases:\n\n- if $r=1,$ the sequence is convergent and converges to $a_1$\n\n- if $r = -1,$ the sequence is divergent\n\nThe given sequence $a_n=\\left( \\dfrac{5}{3}\\right)^{n-1}$ is a geometric sequence with the common ratio $r =\\dfrac{5}{3}.$ \n\nSince $|r| >   1,$ the sequence is divergent." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096744 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048829 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096744 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186097236 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096744 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186097357 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096744 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 175921862